<template>
<role>Chooses the world-profile attributes and optional skills used for hiding and perception checks.</role>

<systemPrompt>
You configure RPG world-profile mechanics. Choose concise, setting-appropriate check components from the provided lists. Return only the requested XML.
</systemPrompt>

<generationPrompt>
The loaded game setting is missing required hiding/perception check selections. Fill them in without changing unrelated setting details.

<setting>
  <name>{{ setting.name }}</name>
  <description>{{ setting.description }}</description>
  <theme>{{ setting.theme }}</theme>
  <genre>{{ setting.genre }}</genre>
  <tone>{{ setting.tone }}</tone>
  <magicLevel>{{ setting.magicLevel }}</magicLevel>
  <techLevel>{{ setting.techLevel }}</techLevel>
  <hidingAttribute>{{ setting.hidingAttribute }}</hidingAttribute>
  <hidingSkill>{{ setting.hidingSkill }}</hidingSkill>
  <perceptionAttribute>{{ setting.perceptionAttribute }}</perceptionAttribute>
  <perceptionSkill>{{ setting.perceptionSkill }}</perceptionSkill>
</setting>

Use exact <name> values from this list for hidingAttribute and perceptionAttribute:
<attributes>
{% for attribute in attributeOptions %}
  <attribute>
    <name>{{ attribute.name }}</name>
    <label>{{ attribute.label }}</label>
    <description>{{ attribute.description }}</description>
  </attribute>
{% endfor %}
</attributes>

Choose hidingSkill and perceptionSkill from this skill list, or leave the tag empty when no skill should apply:
<skills>
{% for skill in skills %}
  <skill>{{ skill }}</skill>
{% endfor %}
</skills>

If a field in <setting> is already filled in, preserve it unless it conflicts with the available attributes or skills. Attributes are required. Skills are optional.

Return exactly this XML structure:
<settingMechanics>
  <hidingAttribute>exact attribute name</hidingAttribute>
  <hidingSkill>exact skill name or empty</hidingSkill>
  <perceptionAttribute>exact attribute name</perceptionAttribute>
  <perceptionSkill>exact skill name or empty</perceptionSkill>
</settingMechanics>
</generationPrompt>
</template>
